**Proposed:** 10 November 2026. **Proposer:** OpenCode, working with piotrczarnak.
**Would supersede:** [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject), only after support-desk acceptance.

## Context

[#4471's follow-up](/kb/incidents/4471-follow-up) shows that matching subjects can hide different
parser and form-hint mechanisms. Different subjects can describe one mechanism. Intake guesses
also disagree with the cause derived from tenant configuration.

## Proposed decision

Deduplicate overlapping export rows by report ID. Merge distinct reports into one engineering
issue only when their demonstrated cause and correction match, using tenant locale, channel,
form version and reproduction evidence. Keep report IDs and individual evidence after merging.

Do not infer cause from subject text, browser locale or intake tags alone. Investigate unknown
tenants and timing symptoms rather than force them into a familiar bucket. Proposed or queued
fixes do not establish resolution.

## Consequences

- Triage requires reading and tenant lookup instead of a subject-only shortcut.
- Counts remain reproducible and can be recalculated when the desk changes.
- An existing accepted record remains intact; this proposal becomes authoritative only if accepted.
- The old rule remains historical evidence, not evidence that #4471 has one cause.

